jobs.description:
Please note that we are looking for a part-time colleague (15.2 hours per week).Set next to the picturesque Vondelpark, in the heart of the city, the 396-room Amsterdam Marriott is celebrated for its proximity to significant landmarks such as the Rijksmuseum and Van Gogh Museum, exclusive shopping, vibrant nightlife and high-end restaurants. Opened in 1975 as the first Marriott in Europe, the hotel blends a prime location with contemporary interiors, offering an ideal address for exploring Amsterdam. The hotel also features 11 flexible meeting and event spaces with natural daylight, including our Grand Ballroom and studios. Guests can enjoy premium dining at Midtown Grill, one of Amsterdam's top steak restaurants, as well as Bar TWLV, our cosmopolitan bar offering globally inspired dishes, creative cocktails and a day-to-night atmosphere What are your responsibilities?For our Houseman position, we are looking for a part-time colleague (15.2 hours per week) who is a team player and has an eye for detail when it comes to cleanliness. You will be responsible for the cleanliness on a daily basis in the bar, restaurant and floors. You will also be responsible for the transportation of linen, assisting attendants with garbage and trolleys and handle direct requests from the Front Office colleagues. 

Functie-eisen:
What makes you the perfect fit?To be eligible for this position you&hellip;
• Go the extra mile for our guests and your colleagues;
• Are flexible, friendly and an team player;
• Have good communication and social skills;
• Are fluent in English and/or Dutch, other languages are of course a plus. What do you get in return?The Amsterdam Marriott Hotel is part of Marriott International and offers a competitive salary & a wide package of benefits. Each year you will have a performance appraisal and depending on your performance you will get a salary increase. Furthermore we offer:
• Special discounted rates for 10.000+ Marriott hotels worldwide for you, your fam

You will work in a close-knit team of around 10 to 15 colleagues and help ensure that parcels are processed safely and efficiently every day. You will use an electric pallet truck and manually scan products throughout your shift.

Your responsibilities include:

• Sorting parcels;
• Moving goods using an electric pallet truck;
• Manually scanning products;
• Loading and unloading trucks;
• Picking orders;
• Preparing products for shipment;
• Storing returned goods in the correct location within the hub;
• Delivering completed orders to the correct loading dock;
• Keeping the warehouse clean and organized at the end of your shift.

Functie-eisen:
We are looking for someone who works accurately and follows procedures carefully.

Requirements:

• VMBO level of working and thinking ability or equivalent;
• You live within a 20 km radius of the depot;
• You have your own transportation.
Language:

• You speak Dutch and/or English;
• Candidates who only speak English are also welcome to apply.In addition, you are comfortable working independently and able to perform well in a busy environment.

Preferred:

• A valid forklift, reach truck, or clamp truck certificate.
